      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco, O-28, pujar">|FRAME: CPD-9307 &quot;(+)-&lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-Isoalliin&quot;| is the precursor of the onion lacrimatory-factor |FRAME: CPD-9305|. It was first isolated and characterized in 1961 |CITS: [Virtanen61]|, and the stereo configuration of the double bond was reported a few years later |CITS: [Carson66]|. While it is still not clear how |FRAME: CPD-9307| is formed, it seems that &amp;gamma;-glutamyl peptides are not the immediate precursors for its synthesis |CITS: [Edwards94]|.</Comment>
